  "title": "Erdős Problem #514",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(z)$ be an entire transcendental function. Does there exist a path $L$ so that, for every $n$, $ \\lvert f(z)/z^n\\rvert \\to \\infty $ as $z\\to \\infty$ along $L$?\nCan the length of this path be estimated in terms of $M(r)=\\max_{\\lvert z\\rvert=r}\\lvert f(z)\\rvert$? Does there exist a path along which $\\lvert f(z)\\rvert$ tends to $\\infty$ faster than a fixed function of $M(r)$ (such that $M(r)^\\epsilon$)?",
